    {
      "id": "bar-m2-tbs7-ex1",
      "title": "Goodwill",
      "html": "<p>Reporting-unit carrying amount $1,500,000 includes goodwill $300,000. Fair value is $1,280,000. For this exercise impairment equals the excess capped at goodwill.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "bar-m2-tbs7-ex2",
      "title": "Software policy",
      "html": "<p>Under the applicable policy, development costs of $90,000 qualify for capitalization. Training $12,000 and maintenance $8,000 are expensed. Ignore amortization for this period.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Goodwill impairment</h3><p>$1,500,000 − $1,280,000 = $220,000, below goodwill of $300,000.</p><h3>Remaining goodwill</h3><p>$300,000 − $220,000 = $80,000.</p><h3>Capitalized software cost</h3><p>Only the $90,000 qualifying development cost is capitalized.</p><h3>Current training and maintenance expense</h3><p>$12,000 + $8,000 = $20,000.</p>"
